{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/119956-lunar-speculation-from-ex3-comic","id":119956,"title":"Lunar speculation (from Ex3 comic)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-26T14:11:44-07:00","id":119956,"title":"Lunar speculation (from Ex3 comic)","content":"I'll start things off.<br /> <br /> I think that our Spider Lunar was a Casteless trying to earn her Full Moon stripes by defeating Visiting Flare. Hence the lack of tattoos and insistence upon defeating the Dawn Caste in a fair fight.<br /> In the previous editions the Casteless phase of a Lunar's life was confined entirely to their origin story unless the player was really determined to play a weaker character. Given that 3rd edition PCs start at essence 1 this might be a sign that Lunars will be encouraged to play out earning their Castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T14:27:22-07:00","id":119969,"title":"","content":"She survived getting cut completely in half by turning into a bird (sans legs). So perhaps an a ability to negate potentially lethal damage through shape-shifting? Also spider filaments to hold weapons those are pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","user":"Calboon","date":". 04-26-2014, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T15:01:44-07:00","id":119986,"title":"","content":"She also talked about having been <i>trained </i>by Sublime Danger, and given a higher purpose by her as well (I think; the wording was a little ambiguous). This makes me wonder if 3E will do more for the Silver Pact's mentoring arrangements. Earlier editions all but outright told you that you were Roleplaying A Lunar Incorrectly if your PC didn't have a Mentor-with-a-capital-M, defined by taking dots in the Background of the same name - but at the same time, gave you, the <i>player</i>, very little incentive to <i>want </i>such a relationship.<br /> <br /> All it really opened up was Sorcery, and then only the good stuff if you were a No-Moon and willing to put yourself increasingly in debt to what could very probably turn out to be a pretty breathtakingly-awful person. Oh, and I guess maybe some MA styles? I don't know, 2E just <i>really </i>didn't do a good job of selling it as any kind of beneficial arrangement for the PC for all that the fluff hammered on it, and that's a real shame in a setting where old masters with ancient mystical wisdom and epic vendettas against other old masters are such a staple of the genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T16:38:18-07:00","id":120022,"title":"","content":"I'm betting Spider Lunar is a chimera, at least. Possibly casteless, although if she is casteless, it's by choice. I wouldn't assume that Lunar castes and the moonsilver tattoos always go together. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, Spider Lunar was there for &quot;all swords,&quot; so her objective isn't Visiting Flare exclusively; he was just the first stop. She was told exactly where to wait for the Sword Priest and says she was given a higher purpose, so she's not there because of Rakan Thulio's curse, although she is most likely aware of it. She's dreamed of defeating the Sword Priest, which suggests she's known about him for more than a few weeks, which is how long Visiting Flare has been Exalted. Visiting Flare comments that she &quot;thinks swordsmanship is found in a test of strength,&quot; which suggests that her swordsmanship isn't actually very good. <br /> <br /> My guess is, Sublime Danger was a First Age Lunar and Eternal Nova's mate. She trained Spider Lunar in swordsmanship, but would not shut up about the Sword Priest, to the point where Spider Lunar became jealous of him. Sublime Danger learned of Eternal Nova's reincarnation through Rakan Thulio's curse and sent Spider Lunar out to fight him in order to awaken Visiting Flare's memory of her and so Spider Lunar would witness the supreme swordsmanship of the Sword Priest and hopefully get over her jealousy. Sublime Danger expected Spider Lunar to survive, but certainly not to win. Spider Lunar probably thought that defeating the Sword Priest would mark the completion of her training, but Sublime Danger most likely organized the fight to serve as another lesson for her student.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T16:49:04-07:00","id":120027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/119956-lunar-speculation-from-ex3-comic?p=120022#post120022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm betting Spider Lunar is a chimera, at least. Possibly casteless, although if she is casteless, it's by choice. I wouldn't assume that Lunar castes and the moonsilver tattoos always go together.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - we've been told that Chimerae won't be as they were in 2e.<br /> <br /> 2 - Her anima didn't flare, and she was in disguise mode, so her tattoos reasonably might not show, either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T07:50:42-07:00","id":120333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/119956-lunar-speculation-from-ex3-comic?p=120022#post120022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond that, Spider Lunar was there for &quot;all swords,&quot; so her objective isn't Visiting Flare exclusively; he was just the first stop. She was told exactly where to wait for the Sword Priest and says she was given a higher purpose, so she's not there because of Rakan Thulio's curse, although she is most likely aware of it. She's dreamed of defeating the Sword Priest, which suggests she's known about him for more than a few weeks, which is how long Visiting Flare has been Exalted. Visiting Flare comments that she &quot;thinks swordsmanship is found in a test of strength,&quot; which suggests that her swordsmanship isn't actually very good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I just took that to refer to Thulio's promise of &quot;Kill the Sword Priest, become the Sword Priest - act now, and get his mystic power over swords free with purchase!&quot; That'd actually be something neat to see in 3E - fighting the old master so you can be the new master, and get some perks to go with the spiffy new title. As for Visiting Flare being disdainful of Moonspider for &quot;thinking swordsmanship is found in a test of strength,&quot; I suspect that might just be a genre conceit in action - does one fighter have more gross physical strength than the other? Is it made visually-obvious that this is the case, with huge muscles or an overtly-inhuman appearance? Is this disparity commented upon by the fighters or by onlookers (this one is especially important)? Yeah, you know they gonna lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T07:54:04-07:00","id":120336,"title":"","content":"My guess?<br /> <br /> She wasn't actually a Lunar at all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:03:45-07:00","id":120395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/119956-lunar-speculation-from-ex3-comic?p=120333#post120333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Visiting Flare being disdainful of Moonspider for &quot;thinking swordsmanship is found in a test of strength,&quot; I suspect that might just be a genre conceit in action - does one fighter have more gross physical strength than the other? Is it made visually-obvious that this is the case, with huge muscles or an overtly-inhuman appearance? Is this disparity commented upon by the fighters or by onlookers (this one is especially important)? Yeah, you know they gonna lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, I figured it was because Moonspider was using her Strength Charms to crush our boy in that swordpress move, and he couldn't hack it, so he used that line to rattle her and make her lose focus, make her subconsciously hold back so she could demonstrate her superior &quot;skill&quot;, not a thing you wanna do against a Solar, rather than focus on winning the fight, skill be damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T10:23:52-07:00","id":120401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/119956-lunar-speculation-from-ex3-comic?p=120395#post120395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hah, I figured it was because Moonspider was using her Strength Charms to crush our boy in that swordpress move, and he couldn't hack it, so he used that line to rattle her and make her lose focus, make her subconsciously hold back so she could demonstrate her superior &quot;skill&quot;, not a thing you wanna do against a Solar, rather than focus on winning the fight, skill be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I wouldn't mind that at all, especially if it means that in another take, another campaign, his attempt at baiting her might have turned out more like <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0827.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.*<br /> <br /> *To be clear, I mean in the sense that taking on a Lunar who knows what they're doing should be a prospect to give anyone at least a <i>little </i>pause, not in the dumb, &quot;FUCK YOU SOLARS&quot; sense. The writing in earlier editions sometimes had a way of making it feel like a Lunar just couldn't win, no matter what they were up against, so I'd be glad to see that change.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:13:56-07:00","id":120414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/119956-lunar-speculation-from-ex3-comic?p=120395#post120395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, I figured it was because Moonspider was using her Strength Charms to crush our boy in that swordpress move, and he couldn't hack it, so he used that line to rattle her and make her lose focus, make her subconsciously hold back so she could demonstrate her superior &quot;skill&quot;, not a thing you wanna do against a Solar, rather than focus on winning the fight, skill be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took this a bit differently. We know the new combat system is designed about building up leverage for a big finish, but we also know you can attack with little to know leverage for small wounds. I took the comment &quot;thinking swordsmanship is found in a test of strength&quot; to mean the the Moonspider was pushing for a quick win. Meaning she was forcing attacks without any real leverage and possibly using charms to try and boost damage with no real leverage. Where Visiting Flare built up his leverage and used a big attack to cleave her in half. Only her shape-changing managed to save her... Lunars were always a pain in the arse to kill!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:20:55-07:00","id":120416,"title":"","content":"Constantly going for the kill without attempting to create openings does seem to sum up her approach. I think she only ever got in a hit when an opening just happened to exist for her to exploit, such after he failed to bind her with the yo-yo, or when that vision distracted him. She was reckless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}